{"timestamp":"2026-05-30T03:09:39.582Z","level":"info","source":"model","message":"response","data":{"model":"qwen36-35b","text":"\n\nI've loaded the **VoidRift Blueprint** (`blueprint.md`). Here's a summary of what this document defines:\n\n---\n\n## VoidRift: Decoupled Subsystem Architecture\n\nVoidRift is a **highly decoupled, model-agnostic monorepo AI engineering harness** designed as a local developer tool. It combines a multi-agent orchestrator with a React/Ink-based Terminal User Interface (TUI).\n\n### Key Philosophy\n- **Local-First & Model Agnostic**: Runs local open-weight models (Ollama, vLLM, Llama.cpp) and cloud models (DeepSeek, Gemini, Anthropic, OpenAI)\n- **No rate limits or cloud lock-in**\n- **$0 cost for local loops** with pennies per session for cloud routing\n\n### Five Architectural Pillars\n1. **Pure Composition Root & Event Bus** — Subsystems communicate via a central async Event Bus, never directly\n2. **Three-Partition Context** — Static *Governance*, semi-dynamic *Workspace*, volatile *Work* (up to 90% prompt cache reuse)\n3. **Path-Mutex Concurrency Scheduler** — Git worktrees with lock ledger for 10","toolCalls":[],"usage":{"promptTokens":4653,"completionTokens":676,"totalTokens":5329}}}
